dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.mem.class]/1: a member class of a class template may be
defined outside the class template definition (`template <class C> class
stream<C>::sentry { ... };').  Declared in the class (`class sentry;') and
used in a member function defined after that definition, `sentry
cerb(*this)' must find the out-of-class definition's explicit constructor
`sentry(stream<C> &)'.  The front end instead sees an incomplete or
constructor-less `sentry' ("invalid implicit conversion from 'struct
stream' to 'struct sentry'"), drops the member function and verifies a
wrong result.  This is the stream `sentry' of both standard libraries:
libstdc++'s basic_ostream::sentry / basic_istream::sentry (ostream,
istream: tellp, put, flush, read, __ostream_insert -- 3 descs in the
round-163 audit, e.g. `in.read(buf, 3)' yields a wrong gcount()) and
libc++'s basic_ostream::sentry (ostream:259-287, 3 descs).  Header-free.
Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51 fails the same way).
